window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-horikita-manabu"]=[{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v1-p66-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu club fair debut  absolute presence student council president  takes the stage at the club fair  school gymnasium club fair  representatives from various athletic and cultural clubs deliver lively pitches  student council president horikita manabu steps onto the stage  slender build  sharp analytical gaze behind glasses  neatly trimmed black hair  merely by stepping up to the microphone  his sheer aura and commanding presence reduce over a hundred chattering first year students to dead  breathless silence without him saying a single word or raising a hand   i m the student council president  my name is horikita manabu   the student council is looking to recruit potential candidates among the first year students to replace the graduating third years  although no special qualifications are required for candidacy  we humbly ask that those considering application not be involved in other club activities  we generally do not accept students involved elsewhere   furthermore  we in the student council do not wish to appoint anyone who possesses a naive outlook  not only would such a person not be elected  he or she would sully the sanctity of this school  it is the student council s right and duty to enforce and amend the rules  but the school expects more than that  we gladly welcome those of you who understand this  delivers his speech in a quiet  eloquent  razor sharp monotone without pausing once  immediately hops off the stage and walks out of the gymnasium  leaving the room paralyzed with intimidation  unmatched psychological dominance and institutional authority  commands immediate  involuntary deference from the entire freshman class  austere  aristocratic  intensely disciplined  zero warmth or theatricality  speaks with absolute executive authority  student council membership condition  absolute commitment  members are prohibited from participating in any other school club","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v1-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Club Fair debut: absolute presence<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.66–68<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">School gymnasium club fair. Representatives from various athletic and cultural clubs deliver lively pitches. Student council president Horikita Manabu steps onto the stage.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m the student council president. My name is Horikita Manabu.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“The student council is looking to recruit potential candidates among the first-year students to replace the graduating third years. Although no special qualifications are required for candidacy, we humbly ask that those…”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Furthermore, we in the student council do not wish to appoint anyone who possesses a naive outlook. Not only would such a person not be elected, he or she would sully the sanctity of this school. It is the student council’s…”<span class=\"pg\">p.67–68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Student Council President; takes the stage at the club fair.<span class=\"pg\">p.66–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Slender build, sharp analytical gaze behind glasses, neatly trimmed black hair. Merely by stepping up to the microphone, his sheer aura and commanding presence reduce over a hundred chattering first-year students to dead, breathless silence without him saying a single word or raising a hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.66–67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The student council is looking to recruit potential candidates among the first-year students to replace the graduating third years. Although no special qualifications are required for candidacy, we humbly ask that those considering application not be involved in other club activities. We generally do not accept students involved elsewhere.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Furthermore, we in the student council do not wish to appoint anyone who possesses a naive outlook. Not only would such a person not be elected, he or she would sully the sanctity of this school. It is the student council’s right and duty to enforce and amend the rules, but the school expects more than that. We gladly welcome those of you who understand this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Delivers his speech in a quiet, eloquent, razor-sharp monotone without pausing once. Immediately hops off the stage and walks out of the gymnasium, leaving the room paralyzed with intimidation.<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Unmatched psychological dominance and institutional authority; commands immediate, involuntary deference from the entire freshman class.<span class=\"pg\">p.66–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Austere, aristocratic, intensely disciplined, zero warmth or theatricality; speaks with absolute executive authority.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Student Council membership condition: absolute commitment; members are prohibited from participating in any other school club.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v1-p192-1\">→ After: Night confrontation, martial arts brawl, &amp; sizing up Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v1-p192-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu night confrontation  martial arts brawl    sizing up ayanokoji dark pathway outside student dormitories  late night  confronts his younger sister suzune in the dead of night  displays chilling  emotionless detachment  treating her like an insignificant nuisance   suzune  i didn t think you d follow me this far   i heard you were placed in class d  i suppose nothing has really changed in the last three years  you ve always been fixated on following me  and as a result you don t notice your own flaws  choosing to come to this school was a mistake   it s pointless  you will never reach class a  in fact  your class will fall apart soon enough  things at this school aren t as simple as you think  grabs suzune roughly by the wrist and slams her back against the rough concrete wall when she insists she will reach class a   i told you  it s pointless  you really are a disobedient little sister   no matter how i try to avoid you  the fact remains that you re my little sister  if people around here learned the truth  i would be humiliated  leave this school immediately   how incredibly stupid  do you want to relive the pain of the past   you possess neither the abilities nor the qualities needed to reach class a  get that through your head  prepares to violently slam suzune onto the concrete ground  but his right wrist is suddenly intercepted and gripped from behind by ayanokoji   what  you  eavesdropping is not an admirable quality  instantly unleashes a vicious martial combination the second ayanokoji lets go  throws a blinding backhand strike aimed directly at ak s face  followed immediately by a sharp kick targeting an unguarded opening  and reaches out with an open hand to execute a throw  master martial artist  holds  5th dan in karate  and  4th dan in aikido  strikes with enough lethal force and speed to knock an opponent unconscious in a single blow  exhales deeply in slight confusion when ayanokoji evades all strikes and slaps his throw hand away   good reflexes  i didn t imagine you could evade all of my blows so quickly  also  you seemed to understand quite well what i was trying to do  have you been taught  directly penetrates ayanokoji s facade when ak claims he only learned piano and calligraphy  delivers a biting philosophical diagnosis to suzune and a parting assessment to ak   you re in class d  too  aren t you  what a unique boy  suzune   suzune  is this boy your friend  i m honestly surprised   you continue to confuse independence with solitude  and you  ayanokouji  with you around  things might get interesting  uncompromising perfectionist  views weakness and familial dependency with icy disgust  highly perceptive judge of martial and psychological capability  older brother  regards her as a humiliating  inferior shadow desperately chasing him  demands she withdraw from school  immediately recognizes an extraordinary individual capable of reacting to and neutralizing high dan martial techniques","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v1-p192-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Night confrontation, martial arts brawl, &amp; sizing up Ayanokōji<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.192–196<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Dark pathway outside student dormitories, late night.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Suzune. I didn’t think you’d follow me this far.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I heard you were placed in Class D. I suppose nothing has really changed in the last three years. You’ve always been fixated on following me, and as a result you don’t notice your own flaws. Choosing to come to this school was a…”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s pointless. You will never reach Class A. In fact, your class will fall apart soon enough. Things at this school aren’t as simple as you think.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Confronts his younger sister Suzune in the dead of night; displays chilling, emotionless detachment, treating her like an insignificant nuisance.<span class=\"pg\">p.192–193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I heard you were placed in Class D. I suppose nothing has really changed in the last three years. You’ve always been fixated on following me, and as a result you don’t notice your own flaws. Choosing to come to this school was a mistake.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Grabs Suzune roughly by the wrist and slams her back against the rough concrete wall when she insists she will reach Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I told you, it’s pointless. You really are a disobedient little sister.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No matter how I try to avoid you, the fact remains that you’re my little sister. If people around here learned the truth, I would be humiliated. Leave this school immediately.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How incredibly stupid. Do you want to relive the pain of the past?”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You possess neither the abilities nor the qualities needed to reach Class A. Get that through your head.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Prepares to violently slam Suzune onto the concrete ground, but his right wrist is suddenly intercepted and gripped from behind by Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.193–194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What? You… Eavesdropping is not an admirable quality.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Instantly unleashes a vicious martial combination the second Ayanokōji lets go: throws a blinding backhand strike aimed directly at AK’s face, followed immediately by a sharp kick targeting an unguarded opening, and reaches out with an open hand to execute a throw.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Master martial artist: holds **5th dan in karate** and **4th dan in aikido**; strikes with enough lethal force and speed to knock an opponent unconscious in a single blow.<span class=\"pg\">p.194, 196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Exhales deeply in slight confusion when Ayanokōji evades all strikes and slaps his throw hand away.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Good reflexes. I didn’t imagine you could evade all of my blows so quickly. Also, you seemed to understand quite well what I was trying to do. Have you been taught?”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Directly penetrates Ayanokōji&#x27;s facade when AK claims he only learned piano and calligraphy. Delivers a biting philosophical diagnosis to Suzune and a parting assessment to AK.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re in Class D, too, aren’t you? What a unique boy, Suzune.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Suzune, is this boy your friend? I’m honestly surprised.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You continue to confuse independence with solitude. And you, Ayanokouji. With you around, things might get interesting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Uncompromising perfectionist; views weakness and familial dependency with icy disgust; highly perceptive judge of martial and psychological capability.<span class=\"pg\">p.192–196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Older brother; regards her as a humiliating, inferior shadow desperately chasing him; demands she withdraw from school.<span class=\"pg\">p.192–193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Immediately recognizes an extraordinary individual capable of reacting to and neutralizing high-dan martial techniques.<span class=\"pg\">p.193–196<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v1-p66-1\">← Before: Club Fair debut: absolute presence<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p193-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6  6 1  the president at the head of the table the student council room on the fourth floor  he sits in the back and does not look at his sister as she enters   because i am quite busy  there are certain agenda topics upon which i will defer  as a general rule  though  i would prefer to attend to these issues  as i m entrusted to lead this student council  chabashira s probe about whether his presence is chance does not move him at all  the narrator notes his record   class a on entry  student council secretary  president by december of his first year on an overwhelming vote   it would seem there s no objection  given the arguments we ve heard thus far   regardless which party called the other over  the fact remains that it was a one sided fight between sudou and the other students  we can clearly see that from the injuries they sustained  we have no choice but to come up with a conclusion based on that  he decides the case on visible injuries and closes the evidentiary question before class d has finished speaking  the narrator describes his intervention as wanting  to draw a conclusion as soon as possible","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p193-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: the president at the head of the table<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.193–196<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The student council room on the fourth floor; he sits in the back and does not look at his sister as she enters.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Because I am quite busy, there are certain agenda topics upon which I will defer. As a general rule, though, I would prefer to attend to these issues, as I’m entrusted to lead this student council.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It would seem there’s no objection, given the arguments we’ve heard thus far.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Regardless which party called the other over, the fact remains that it was a one-sided fight between Sudou and the other students. We can clearly see that from the injuries they sustained. We have no choice but to come up with a…<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Chabashira’s probe about whether his presence is chance does not move him at all; the narrator notes his record — Class A on entry, student council secretary, president by December of his first year on an overwhelming vote.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Regardless which party called the other over, the fact remains that it was a one-sided fight between Sudou and the other students. We can clearly see that from the injuries they sustained. We have no choice but to come up with a conclusion based on that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He decides the case on visible injuries and closes the evidentiary question before Class D has finished speaking; the narrator describes his intervention as wanting &quot;to draw a conclusion as soon as possible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p199-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: witness and photograph<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p199-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6  6 1  witness and photograph  are you finished with your claims now  class d  the question lands after horikita s martial arts argument and is described as  few and icy  carrying the implication that class d should have said nothing   i ll allow it  however  please answer more quickly next time   i ll allow it   but sakagami sensei  don t you think this photo is different  he is the one who spots the decisive photograph among the set and slides it across to sakagami  converting sakura s self portraits into evidence of the fight   thank you  sakura san  the thanks is the only courtesy the hearing gives her before the cross examination resumes","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p199-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: witness and photograph<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.199–204<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Are you finished with your claims now, Class D?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’ll allow it. However, please answer more quickly next time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’ll allow it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The question lands after Horikita’s martial-arts argument and is described as &quot;few and icy,&quot; carrying the implication that Class D should have said nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But Sakagami-sensei, don’t you think this photo is different?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> He is the one who spots the decisive photograph among the set and slides it across to Sakagami, converting Sakura’s self-portraits into evidence of the fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Thank you, Sakura-san.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The thanks is the only courtesy the hearing gives her before the cross-examination resumes.<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p193-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: the president at the head of the table<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p208-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: the retrial and the expulsion warning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p208-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6  6 1  the retrial and the expulsion warning  so then what do you mean  it is the first time he looks directly at his sister in the hearing   that s enough  continuing this discussion would just be a waste of time   what i ve learned today is that each side has an exact opposite claim  in that case  one side is propagating an extremely malicious falsehood   i ll ask you  class c  have you lied to us today   well  what about you  class d   then we will regroup here for a retrial tomorrow at 4 00 pm  if by then it hasn t been clearly established which party has lied  or in the event no one admits that they were at fault  we will pass judgment based on the evidence we ve collected thus far  of course  in that case we may have to consider the possibility of expulsion from this school  that is all  the retrial is set for 4 00 pm the next day  and if neither side is proven to have lied or admits fault  judgment falls back on the collected evidence with expulsion as a possible outcome  the escalation is deliberate  the charge shifts from a fight to which class lied to the school","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p208-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: the retrial and the expulsion warning<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.208–209<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;So then…what do you mean?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That’s enough. Continuing this discussion would just be a waste of time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What I’ve learned today is that each side has an exact opposite claim. In that case, one side is propagating an extremely malicious falsehood.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> It is the first time he looks directly at his sister in the hearing.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’ll ask you, Class C. Have you lied to us today?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, what about you, Class D?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then we will regroup here for a retrial tomorrow at 4:00 PM. If by then it hasn’t been clearly established which party has lied, or in the event no one admits that they were at fault, we will pass judgment based on the evidence we’ve collected thus far. Of course, in that case we may have to consider the possibility of expulsion from this school. That is all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The retrial is set for 4:00 PM the next day, and if neither side is proven to have lied or admits fault, judgment falls back on the collected evidence with expulsion as a possible outcome.<span class=\"pg\">p.208–209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The escalation is deliberate: the charge shifts from a fight to which class lied to the school.<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p199-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: witness and photograph<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p210-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: the corridor conversation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p210-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6  6 1  the corridor conversation  you re still here   what are you planning to do   i thought that when you came here with suzune  you d unveil some kind of master plan   so does that mean when suzune claimed sudou was completely innocent  she was merely getting carried away   i see   then there s what you said  sakura   eyewitness testimony and pictorial evidence certainly carry weight during deliberation  however  please keep in mind that how much we value the evidence is determined by how much we trust in its believability  no matter what you do  the evidence s legitimacy is reduced because you are a student from class d  no matter how detailed your account  we cannot accept it as one hundred percent true   if you can t prove it  then it s little more than nonsense   since she s a class d student  it s only natural that you would want to believe her   so can you prove it  can you prove she s not lying  the narrator s revised estimate  the first meeting left a bad impression  but  i found him easy to talk to now  and he credits  a superior understanding of human nature  he  chuckled softly  then smiled  at the claim that suzune will prove it   the chapter does not say whether the smile is disbelief or interest  he ignores her until she refuses to sit  then asks her meaning and listens  the hearing is the first time he treats her as an opponent rather than a disappointment  he thanks her for the photograph and then tells her the evidence cannot be accepted because of where she is enrolled  the corridor exchange is the longest conversation they have had  he tests whether the narrator has a plan and accepts the answer that suzune will supply it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p210-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: the corridor conversation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.210–212<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You’re still here?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What are you planning to do?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I thought that when you came here with Suzune, you’d unveil some kind of master plan.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So does that mean when Suzune claimed Sudou was completely innocent, she was merely getting carried away?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then there’s what you said, Sakura.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Eyewitness testimony and pictorial evidence certainly carry weight during deliberation. However, please keep in mind that how much we value the evidence is determined by how much we trust in its believability. No matter what you do, the evidence’s legitimacy is reduced because you are a student from Class D. No matter how detailed your account, we cannot accept it as one hundred percent true.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you can’t prove it, then it’s little more than nonsense.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Since she’s a Class D student, it’s only natural that you would want to believe her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So can you prove it? Can you prove she’s not lying?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narrator’s revised estimate: the first meeting left a bad impression, but &quot;I found him easy to talk to now,&quot; and he credits &quot;a superior understanding of human nature.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He &quot;chuckled softly, then smiled&quot; at the claim that Suzune will prove it — the chapter does not say whether the smile is disbelief or interest.<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He ignores her until she refuses to sit, then asks her meaning and listens; the hearing is the first time he treats her as an opponent rather than a disappointment.<span class=\"pg\">p.193–208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> He thanks her for the photograph and then tells her the evidence cannot be accepted because of where she is enrolled.<span class=\"pg\">p.204–211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The corridor exchange is the longest conversation they have had; he tests whether the narrator has a plan and accepts the answer that Suzune will supply it.<span class=\"pg\">p.210–212<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p208-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: the retrial and the expulsion warning<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p244-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.5: the withdrawal ruling<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p244-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 7  7 5  the withdrawal ruling  did you want to come to an agreement  or did you already do something to the effect  he gazes sharply at the class c students while they signal that they do not want to compromise   if you wish to withdraw your complaint  we have no intention of fighting it  we accept  the regulations line that demands a point payment for the deliberation expenses is printed with no speaker attached   very well  the proceedings have come to an end  we will now call this discussion closed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p244-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.5: the withdrawal ruling<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.244–246<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Did you want to come to an agreement? Or did you already do something to the effect?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you wish to withdraw your complaint, we have no intention of fighting it. We accept.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Very well, the proceedings have come to an end. We will now call this discussion closed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He gazes sharply at the Class C students while they signal that they do not want to compromise.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The regulations line that demands a point payment for the deliberation expenses is printed with no speaker attached.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p210-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: the corridor conversation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p252-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.6: the thanks, and the secretary seat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p252-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 7  7 6  the thanks  and the secretary seat  excellent work   i have approved class c s request to withdraw their complaint   so this was all to prove that sakura wasn t a liar  as you said  i suppose if class c withdrew their complaint  then talk would spread quite naturally  if sudou or sakura weren t the liars  then class c was  he stops in his tracks to address ayanokoji instead of exchanging a light greeting  and stays still while he is looked at   tachibana  do you still have one seat open for secretary   ayanokouji  if you wanted it  i would appoint you to the position   do you disapprove  he spells out the result as the proof of her credibility  with the withdrawal  class c becomes the liar  he offers him the secretary position on the spot  the offer is refused without discussion","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p252-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.6: the thanks, and the secretary seat<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.252–253<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Excellent work.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I have approved Class C’s request to withdraw their complaint.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;So this was all to prove that Sakura wasn’t a liar, as you said? I suppose if Class C withdrew their complaint, then talk would spread quite naturally. If Sudou or Sakura weren’t the liars, then Class C was.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He stops in his tracks to address Ayanokōji instead of exchanging a light greeting, and stays still while he is looked at.<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Tachibana. Do you still have one seat open for secretary?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji. If you wanted it, I would appoint you to the position.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you disapprove?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> He spells out the result as the proof of her credibility: with the withdrawal, Class C becomes the liar.<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He offers him the secretary position on the spot; the offer is refused without discussion.<span class=\"pg\">p.252–253<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p244-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.5: the withdrawal ruling<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p62-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 3  passing mentions manabu surfaces in the birthday hunt as the one person who might know his sister s date  the student council president is named outright while sudou shrugs off his own ignorance  a line records that thirty minutes have passed since a conversation with horikita s older brother","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p62-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.62–63, 74<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Manabu surfaces in the birthday hunt as the one person who might know his sister&#x27;s date.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The student council president is named outright while Sudou shrugs off his own ignorance.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A line records that thirty minutes have passed since a conversation with Horikita&#x27;s older brother.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p67-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the crossroads conversation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p67-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 3  the crossroads conversation manabu and tachibana intercept ak at the dorm crossroads during their student council reorganizing work   it s been a while  he invites ak to accompany him and will not take no for an answer  even after the semester begins   ayanokouji  if you have no prior engagements  i d like you to accompany me   whenever you re free is fine  he has the island and ship test results  including that the rabbit vip avoided detection   information the homeroom teachers lack   i know that you outsmarted the other classes on the island  and that class d s vip in the rabbit group successfully avoided detection   in the end  the leader s name was changed to yours  he credits suzune with the island win in public  then denies she could have devised it   she d never think of something like that  he judges his sister in one line  a failure who belongs in class d   she s a failure who belongs in class d  ak concludes manabu watches him for the same reason as chabashira   the 50  scores and the resume gap  he offers ak the vice presidency  a second vice president is permitted  though only one is typical   will you join the student council   ayanokouji  if you wish  i ll appoint you vice president   there can be two student council vice presidents  he expects the school to change for the worse next year   tachibana reads it as the nagumo presidency   when the time comes  i ll need the power to combat that change  he accepts the refusal  offers the student council room and tea  and withdraws   please feel free to stop by the student council whenever you like  ak reads him as wrestling with his own anxieties despite the office","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p67-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the crossroads conversation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.67–73<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Manabu and Tachibana intercept AK at the dorm crossroads during their student council reorganizing work.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s been a while.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ayanokouji, if you have no prior engagements, I’d like you to accompany me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Whenever you’re free is fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> He invites AK to accompany him and will not take no for an answer, even after the semester begins.<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> He has the island and ship test results, including that the Rabbit VIP avoided detection — information the homeroom teachers lack.<span class=\"pg\">p.69–70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know that you outsmarted the other classes on the island, and that Class D’s VIP in the Rabbit group successfully avoided detection,”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In the end, the leader’s name was changed to yours.”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He credits Suzune with the island win in public, then denies she could have devised it.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’d never think of something like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He judges his sister in one line: a failure who belongs in Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’s a failure who belongs in Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> AK concludes Manabu watches him for the same reason as Chabashira — the 50% scores and the resume gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> He offers AK the vice presidency; a second vice president is permitted, though only one is typical.<span class=\"pg\">p.71–72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Will you join the student council?”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji, if you wish, I’ll appoint you vice president,”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There can be two student council vice presidents.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> He expects the school to change for the worse next year — Tachibana reads it as the Nagumo presidency.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When the time comes, I’ll need the power to combat that change.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He accepts the refusal, offers the student council room and tea, and withdraws.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please feel free to stop by the student council whenever you like.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> AK reads him as wrestling with his own anxieties despite the office.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p62-1\">← Before: Ch.3: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p90-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the council desk with Katsuragi<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p90-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 3  the council desk with katsuragi he and tachibana greet katsuragi and ak at the council room door  the older horikita notices ak immediately   it would seem we have some unexpected visitors  he explains the renovation absences and hears the outside contact inquiry  outside contact is allowed only for compelling reasons such as severe illness or injury   even if communication is one sided  it s still not permitted  he refuses the package request in a professional manner  tachibana supplies the letters in packages history   the things that are explicitly prohibited can t be easily altered using points  the twin sister orphan story lands  he had been about to dash katsuragi s hopes with complete rejection   if school rules forbid something  you cannot circumvent them  even with points  rejection complete  he tells katsuragi to leave if finished   if you re finished  please leave  ak stays behind and pitches the quiet overlook  he reads the ask immediately   you want to resolve everything without involving the school  he refuses to break rules for katsuragi s sake but names ak s own silence as the tell   i won t violate the rules for his sake   if you think so  you should have told katsuragi about the loophole before he left  he escorts ak out and grants a free hand  officially no meeting  no investigation   even if you act behind the scenes  i won t investigate  whether he later arranged sudou s blind spots is left open on p 104","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p90-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the council desk with Katsuragi<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.90–94<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He and Tachibana greet Katsuragi and AK at the council room door; the older Horikita notices AK immediately.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It would seem we have some unexpected visitors.”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Even if communication is one-sided, it’s still not permitted,”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“The things that are explicitly prohibited can’t be easily altered using points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> He explains the renovation absences and hears the outside-contact inquiry.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Outside contact is allowed only for compelling reasons such as severe illness or injury.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> He refuses the package request in a professional manner; Tachibana supplies the letters-in-packages history.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The twin-sister-orphan story lands; he had been about to dash Katsuragi&#x27;s hopes with complete rejection.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If school rules forbid something, you cannot circumvent them, even with points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Rejection complete, he tells Katsuragi to leave if finished.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you’re finished, please leave.”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> AK stays behind and pitches the quiet overlook; he reads the ask immediately.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You want to resolve everything without involving the school,”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He refuses to break rules for Katsuragi&#x27;s sake but names AK&#x27;s own silence as the tell.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t violate the rules for his sake.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you think so, you should have told Katsuragi about the loophole before he left.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> He escorts AK out and grants a free hand: officially no meeting, no investigation.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if you act behind the scenes, I won’t investigate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Whether he later arranged Sudou&#x27;s blind spots is left open on p.104.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p67-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the crossroads conversation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.6: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p179-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi horikita-suzune horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6  a passing mention the student council president is named again as nagumo s rival and as horikita s brother  without appearing  ichinose calls him possibly the most extraordinary student in the school s whole history and notes the shared last name with horikita  he ran against nagumo in the student council elections and is reported disappointed in this year s first year students  the vice president s rise is framed against his presidency  he might step down in october  his sister praises him in front of others without revealing he is her brother","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.179–181<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The student council president is named again as Nagumo&#x27;s rival and as Horikita&#x27;s brother, without appearing.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Ichinose calls him possibly the most extraordinary student in the school&#x27;s whole history and notes the shared last name with Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> He ran against Nagumo in the student council elections and is reported disappointed in this year&#x27;s first-year students.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> The vice president&#x27;s rise is framed against his presidency; he might step down in October.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> His sister praises him in front of others without revealing he is her brother.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p90-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the council desk with Katsuragi<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p182-1\">→ After: Ch.6: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p182-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6  passing mentions the elder horikita is invoked against his sister s council prospects  a line argues he would not allow her onto a council after he had wanted her expelled  suzune recalls ayanokoji s movements because she had once seen him fight her brother","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p182-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.182, 190<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The elder Horikita is invoked against his sister&#x27;s council prospects.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A line argues he would not allow her onto a council after he had wanted her expelled.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Suzune recalls Ayanokōji&#x27;s movements because she had once seen him fight her brother.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v4_5-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.6: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p17-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 2  a passing mention named when horikita s calm outside masks the panic of seeing her older brother at the festival  she mutters his name under her breath as the president s presence lands on her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.17<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named when Horikita’s calm outside masks the panic of seeing her older brother at the festival.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She mutters his name under her breath as the president’s presence lands on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p26-1\">→ After: Ch.2: passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p26-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune fujimaki horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 2  passing mention named as the third year class a student and student council president suzune is scanning for  he does not take red team command  she has never sought him out first   he always initiates contact   and cannot find him in the four hundred strong crowd  fujimaki s command of the red team makes ayanokoji wonder when the president will make a move","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.26<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the third-year Class A student and student council president Suzune is scanning for; he does not take Red Team command.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"fujimaki.html\">Fujimaki<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She has never sought him out first — he always initiates contact — and cannot find him in the four-hundred-strong crowd.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Fujimaki<\/b> Fujimaki’s command of the Red Team makes Ayanokōji wonder when the president will make a move.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p17-1\">← Before: Ch.2: a passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5: The brother, revealed to the group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune nagumo-miyabi horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 5  5  the brother  revealed to the group horikita s brother is named as the student council president when she asks for the relay anchor   it s because i think my brother is an anchor    the reason the group had been pressing for  nagumo is framed as the candidate whose abilities are on par with the president s  ayanokoji s gloss for the others   the two  aren t really on speaking terms","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5: The brother, revealed to the group<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita’s brother is named as the student council president when she asks for the relay anchor.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “It’s because I think my brother…is an anchor,” — the reason the group had been pressing for.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Nagumo is framed as the candidate whose abilities are on par with the president’s.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Ayanokōji’s gloss for the others — the two “aren’t really on speaking terms.”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p26-1\">← Before: Ch.2: passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p95-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: first again<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p95-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6  6  first again horikita manabu runs in the second group of the third year 100 metre dash as his sister watches  naturally takes first place  she answers ayanokoji s comment as simple fact  her brother is perfect and always number one   that s because my brother is perfect  ayanokoji adds that the president does not care about his little sister s feelings in the slightest   his read  not a page quote","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p95-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: first again<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.95–96<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita Manabu runs in the second group of the third-year 100-metre dash as his sister watches.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “That’s because my brother is perfect.”<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Naturally takes first place.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She answers Ayanokōji’s comment as simple fact: her brother is perfect and always number one.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji adds that the president does not care about his little sister’s feelings in the slightest — his read, not a page quote.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5: The brother, revealed to the group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p135-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p135-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6  6  passing mention horikita keeps staring at her brother during the upperclassmen s cavalry   someone she cannot approach  the distance is both social and physical while she is injured and the class is collapsing  the president does not act on or answer the look on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p135-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.135<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita keeps staring at her brother during the upperclassmen’s cavalry — someone she cannot approach.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The distance is both social and physical while she is injured and the class is collapsing.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The president does not act on or answer the look on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p95-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: first again<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p157-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.2: speaks to Suzune at the entrance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p157-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 7  7 2  speaks to suzune at the entrance walking in with tachibana  manabu stops and asks his sister whether she understands class d s situation  student council president  tachibana  secretary  is with him   do you understand class d s situation right now  one line to his sister  then she says she will not bother him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p157-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.2: speaks to Suzune at the entrance<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.157<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking in with Tachibana, Manabu stops and asks his sister whether she understands Class D’s situation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you understand Class D’s situation right now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Student council president; Tachibana, secretary, is with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> One line to his sister, then she says she will not bother him.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p135-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p178-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8.3: named as the one she runs for<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p178-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 8  8 3  named as the one she runs for horikita tells sudou the prim and proper president is her older brother and why she chases his regard   he s my older brother  far from good because she lacks talent  she chases class a for his respect   that s why i ve been running straight ahead  not caring what anyone else thinks of me  sudou learns the connection only here  after calling the president prim and proper","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p178-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.8 §8.3: named as the one she runs for<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.178<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita tells Sudou the prim-and-proper president is her older brother and why she chases his regard.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “That’s why I’ve been running straight ahead, not caring what anyone else thinks of me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “He’s my older brother.”; far from good because she lacks talent; she chases Class A for his respect.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou learns the connection only here, after calling the president prim-and-proper.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p157-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.2: speaks to Suzune at the entrance<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p183-1\">→ After: Ch.9 §9: the relay one-on-one<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p183-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 9  9  the relay one on one the president runs third year class a s anchor  on the back straight he stops still to race ayanokouji after the first year s challenge  among the chosen elites in the mixed 1200 metre relay   do you seriously plan to change this school  asks nagumo about the meritocracy speech   to think that you re the anchor   i see  i suppose she s struggling to make it through   i ve observed your class   up until a short while ago  i thought there was no hope for you  however  i don t get that impression from you at all in this relay  what happened   i keep an eye on every class  no exceptions   i m not interested in such a fanciful future   you really say some interesting things  i thought you hated standing out or getting involved  why change that now   if you give up your chance at second place in order to race me  i ll accept your challenge  it s not often that a first year and third year have the opportunity to compete like this  is it   you did well  great work  stands still with the baton to wait out ayanokouji s challenge  loses the direct duel after the first year s serious kick  learns from ayanokouji that his sister is what changed class d  no look of surprise","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p183-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.9 §9: the relay one-on-one<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.183–188<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The president runs third-year Class A’s anchor; on the back straight he stops still to race Ayanokouji after the first-year’s challenge.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you seriously plan to change this school?”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“To think that you’re the anchor,”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I see. I suppose she’s struggling to make it through,”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Among the chosen elites in the mixed 1200-metre relay.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Asks Nagumo about the meritocracy speech.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve observed your class,”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Up until a short while ago, I thought there was no hope for you. However, I don’t get that impression from you at all in this relay. What happened?”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I keep an eye on every class. No exceptions,”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not interested in such a fanciful future,”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You really say some interesting things. I thought you hated standing out or getting involved. Why change that now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you give up your chance at second place in order to race me, I’ll accept your challenge. It’s not often that a first-year and third-year have the opportunity to compete like this, is it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You did well. Great work,”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Stands still with the baton to wait out Ayanokouji’s challenge; loses the direct duel after the first-year’s serious kick.<span class=\"pg\">p.187–188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Learns from Ayanokouji that his sister is what changed Class D; no look of surprise.<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p178-1\">← Before: Ch.8 §8.3: named as the one she runs for<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v6-p14-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi horikita-suzune horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 2  outgoing student council president student council election ceremony  he delivers final remarks and steps down so nagumo can be sworn in   i m very proud to have led the student council for nearly two years  i m also quite grateful  thank you all very much  brief  unemotional address delivered as solemn obligation  he retreats to his original position when done  nagumo bows deeply to him and praises him as the most capable president in the school s history   while announcing reforms that deny his election timing  suzune watches him leave the stage without shrinking back  no longer afraid of her brother","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v6-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: outgoing student council president<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.14–15<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Student council election ceremony: he delivers final remarks and steps down so Nagumo can be sworn in.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m very proud to have led the student council for nearly two years. I’m also quite grateful. Thank you all very much”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Brief, unemotional address delivered as solemn obligation; he retreats to his original position when done.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Nagumo bows deeply to him and praises him as the most capable president in the school’s history — while announcing reforms that deny his election timing.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Suzune watches him leave the stage without shrinking back, no longer afraid of her brother.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v6-p70-1\">→ After: Ch.4: contrasted with Ryuuen’s violence<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v6-p70-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi ryuuen-kakeru horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 4  contrasted with ryuuen s violence named as former president horikita when ryuuen contrasts his own violence with student council authority  paired with current president nagumo as the style of authority ryuuen explicitly rejects  this wasn t former president horikita or current president nagumo s style of authority  no dialogue or action from horikita manabu on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v6-p70-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: contrasted with Ryuuen’s violence<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.70<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as former-president Horikita when Ryuuen contrasts his own violence with student-council authority.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Paired with current-president Nagumo as the style of authority Ryuuen explicitly rejects.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> This wasn’t former-president Horikita or current-president Nagumo’s style of authority.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No dialogue or action from Horikita Manabu on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v6-p14-1\">← Before: Ch.2: outgoing student council president<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v6-p120-1\">→ After: Ch.5: summoned as the bet’s witness<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v6-p120-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 5  summoned as the bet s witness horikita asks niisan  the former student council president appears as the reliable witness to the mathematics bet  her older brother  she trusts him most at this school  he was called for nothing more than witness   it s been a long time  kushida     i don t forget people    same junior high  but he graduated before the incident   it s been a long time  kushida   do you remember me   i was called to act as witness  nothing more  i m not interested in anything else   she made the bet  it has nothing to do with me   i will fulfill my role as witness  should either of you violate the bet   you d best be prepared for the consequences  after retiring as president he still held great authority  kushida would honour the arrangement until he graduated  no further dialogue on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v6-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: summoned as the bet’s witness<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.120–122<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita asks niisan; the former student council president appears as the reliable witness to the mathematics bet.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s been a long time, Kushida,”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you remember me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I was called to act as witness, nothing more. I’m not interested in anything else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her older brother; she trusts him most at this school; he was called for nothing more than witness.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “It’s been a long time, Kushida.” … “I don’t forget people.” — same junior high, but he graduated before the incident.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She made the bet. It has nothing to do with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I will fulfill my role as witness. Should either of you violate the bet,”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “you’d best be prepared for the consequences.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> After retiring as president he still held great authority; Kushida would honour the arrangement until he graduated.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No further dialogue on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v6-p70-1\">← Before: Ch.4: contrasted with Ryuuen’s violence<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7-p86-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune nagumo-miyabi ichinose-honami katsuragi-kouhei horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 3  the bridge offer buzzer at the first year dorm  former student council president stands in the doorway with no tea taken and a warning about nagumo   i d like a moment of your time  or should i come back later   the second semester ends next week  my time at this school is running out   there s something i wanted to tell you before i leave  about nagumo miyabi   i didn t intend to discuss this with anyone  however  circumstances have changed  i ve adhered to this school s traditions because i believe in its system and rules  nagumo wants to uproot those foundations  most likely  an unprecedented number of students will be expelled next year   you might say that  horikita s brother made no attempt to deny it   i made one mistake after joining the student council  i failed in training my successor  nagumo was the only one i believed had potential  but his ideologies differed from mine  now  he s managed to bring almost all the other second year students under his sway   he s already won over the entire school   why are you giving me all this insider information   if you don t want to draw attention to yourself  use suzune as you ve done in the past  it ll be fine  i ll be the bridge between you and the student council  he told me   you might be right  he must ve known he couldn t cajole me into helping him  but perhaps the elder horikita was so desperate he d swallowed his pride and come here   forgive me for bothering you   what   so  you ll consider it   i expect nothing  but i ll be waiting  private first year room visit  leaves without tea after the number is handed over   use suzune    the bridge runs through her  failed successor  nearly all second years under his sway  the watch target  applicant he refused  then nagumo forcibly seated on the council  the other refused first year applicant  reads the coming expulsion wave and the council coup from inside knowledge  swallows pride enough to visit a first year alone  formal  direct  no tea  admits the successor mistake without flinching  expects nothing and waits","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the bridge offer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.86–89<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Buzzer at the first-year dorm; former student council president stands in the doorway with no tea taken and a warning about Nagumo.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’d like a moment of your time. Or should I come back later?”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“The second semester ends next week. My time at this school is running out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“There’s something I wanted to tell you before I leave. About Nagumo Miyabi.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t intend to discuss this with anyone. However, circumstances have changed. I’ve adhered to this school’s traditions because I believe in its system and rules. Nagumo wants to uproot those foundations. Most likely, an unprecedented number of students will be expelled next year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You might say that.” Horikita’s brother made no attempt to deny it. “I made one mistake after joining the student council. I failed in training my successor. Nagumo was the only one I believed had potential, but his ideologies differed from mine. Now, he’s managed to bring almost all the other second-year students under his sway.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He’s already won over the entire school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why are you giving me all this insider information?”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you don’t want to draw attention to yourself, use Suzune as you’ve done in the past. It’ll be fine. I’ll be the bridge between you and the student council,” he told me.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You might be right.” He must’ve known he couldn’t cajole me into helping him, but perhaps the elder Horikita was so desperate he’d swallowed his pride and come here. “Forgive me for bothering you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What?”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you’ll consider it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I expect nothing, but I’ll be waiting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Private first-year room visit; leaves without tea after the number is handed over.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Use Suzune” — the bridge runs through her.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Failed successor; nearly all second-years under his sway; the watch target.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Applicant he refused, then Nagumo forcibly seated on the council.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The other refused first-year applicant.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the coming expulsion wave and the council coup from inside knowledge; swallows pride enough to visit a first-year alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Formal, direct, no tea; admits the successor mistake without flinching; expects nothing and waits.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–89<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7-p164-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the witness on the stairs<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7-p164-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae horikita-suzune sakayanagi-arisu horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6  the witness on the stairs arrives as the person ayanokoji texted  former student council president  brought in as the rooftop witness   sorry to have kept you waiting  ayanokouji   that s fine  but don t forget our arrangement  ayanokouji   as long as you understand  try to wrap this up quickly  agrees to stop halfway up the stairs a few minutes after ayanokoji heads up   no talk  no punishment  just make sure the class c students see him on the way down  ayanokoji s half of the deal  if he goes back on his word  manabu may forget what happens today  the next best thing to a teacher witness  presence without intervention  arranged in advance  brief  transactional  already committed to the stair post before the fight starts  the former president who keeps his end of a private bargain  the teacher shocked to see him  concludes he will not go to the roof himself  his sister  named in chabashira s question about who goes upstairs  the fallback witness ayanokoji would have used instead","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7-p164-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the witness on the stairs<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.164–165<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives as the person Ayanokōji texted; former student council president, brought in as the rooftop witness.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Sorry to have kept you waiting, Ayanokouji,”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s fine, but don’t forget our arrangement, Ayanokouji,”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“As long as you understand. Try to wrap this up quickly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Agrees to stop halfway up the stairs a few minutes after Ayanokōji heads up — no talk, no punishment, just make sure the Class C students see him on the way down.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji’s half of the deal: if he goes back on his word, Manabu may forget what happens today.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The next-best thing to a teacher-witness: presence without intervention, arranged in advance.<span class=\"pg\">p.164–165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Brief, transactional, already committed to the stair post before the fight starts.<span class=\"pg\">p.164–165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The former president who keeps his end of a private bargain.<span class=\"pg\">p.164–165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> The teacher shocked to see him; concludes he will not go to the roof himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.164–165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> His sister, named in Chabashira’s question about who goes upstairs.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> The fallback witness Ayanokōji would have used instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7-p86-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the bridge offer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7-p191-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the card kept in play<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7-p191-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru chabashira-sae sakayanagi-arisu horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6  the card kept in play still waiting on the stairs  his presence is what blocks ryuuen s report option after the fight  named as the former student council president a few steps below the roof  ayanokoji cites him as the third party witness who makes ryuuen s trap claim impossible   the former student council president is waiting on the stairs as we speak  has promised to keep the rooftop events to himself   one of ayanokoji s two standing restraints on the story  presence alone rewrites the post fight negotiation without ever entering the room  keeps the stairpost to the end  the promise is cited as fact  not hope  the man whose bargain is now load bearing  the threat the stairpost neutralises  the other adult waiting below  the alternate witness still unused","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the card kept in play<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.191–192, 195<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Still waiting on the stairs; his presence is what blocks Ryuuen’s report option after the fight.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Named as the former student council president a few steps below the roof.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji cites him as the third-party witness who makes Ryuuen’s trap-claim impossible.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “The former student council president is waiting on the stairs as we speak.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Has promised to keep the rooftop events to himself — one of Ayanokōji’s two standing restraints on the story.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Presence alone rewrites the post-fight negotiation without ever entering the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.191–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Keeps the stairpost to the end; the promise is cited as fact, not hope.<span class=\"pg\">p.191–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The man whose bargain is now load-bearing.<span class=\"pg\">p.191–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The threat the stairpost neutralises.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> The other adult waiting below.<span class=\"pg\">p.191–192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> The alternate witness still unused.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7-p164-1\">← Before: Ch.6: the witness on the stairs<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7-p201-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the former president named by role<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7-p201-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"","w":"horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 7  the former president named by role passing mention  ryuuen s next day report is timed because the former student council president already knew what happened on the roof   horikita manabu by prior context  the page does not print his name","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7-p201-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the former president named by role<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.201<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Ryuuen’s next-day report is timed because the former student council president already knew what happened on the roof — Horikita Manabu by prior context; the page does not print his name.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7-p191-1\">← Before: Ch.6: the card kept in play<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p12-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 2  the stair witness after the roof named only as  the former student council president  waiting with chabashira when karuizawa left the roof  helped her back to the dorms on kiyotaka s instructions  considerate  no long speech  acting on his instructions","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the stair witness after the roof<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.12<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named only as “the former student council president” waiting with Chabashira when Karuizawa left the roof.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Helped her back to the dorms on Kiyotaka’s instructions; considerate, no long speech.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Acting on his instructions.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p85-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the Nagumo debt and the sister test<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p85-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru tachibana-akane horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 4  the nagumo debt and the sister test arrives punctually at the snow bench  treats ryuuen as coconspirator  briefs ayanokoji on student council power and nagumo   it s no bother  this is a good time for a secret meeting  a good place  too   ayanokouji  do you recall the promise you made when you sought my help earlier   i d like ayanokouji to preserve and maintain order at this school  i don t care by what means   as a matter of fact  seventeen second year students have already been expelled  according to their exit interviews  nagumo was involved in over half the cases   i cannot tell you at the current stage  i can t guarantee their safety if nagumo finds out   the undercover second year   you re thinking about what happens after i graduate  he answered   my sister s incompetent  she always chased after my shadow  she s made it her goal to catch up to me  that s foolish  he spat   i d cooperate   if suzune joined the student council  debts  briefs  and the undercover second year play  admits he knew of suzune since soon after enrollment  the man he wants removed or obstructed  student council expulsions and exam design as the threat  calls her incompetent and a shadow chaser  would cooperate if she joined the council   harsh  not indifferent  coconspirator by ayanokoji s framing  blocked the snow feint   you aren t fit to serve on the student council  secretary context via the brief handoff  kushida later calls her  blocks ryuuen s jab with vision obscured  adjusts glasses  unfazed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p85-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the Nagumo debt and the sister test<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.85–92<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives punctually at the snow bench; treats Ryuuen as coconspirator; briefs Ayanokōji on student-council power and Nagumo.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"tachibana-akane.html\">Tachibana Akane<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s no bother. This is a good time for a secret meeting. A good place, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ayanokouji, do you recall the promise you made when you sought my help earlier?”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’d like Ayanokouji to preserve and maintain order at this school. I don’t care by what means.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As a matter of fact, seventeen second-year students have already been expelled. According to their exit interviews, Nagumo was involved in over half the cases,”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I cannot tell you at the current stage. I can’t guarantee their safety if Nagumo finds out.” (the undercover second year)<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re thinking about what happens after I graduate,” he answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My sister’s incompetent. She always chased after my shadow. She’s made it her goal to catch up to me. That’s foolish,” he spat.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d cooperate.” (if Suzune joined the student council)<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Debts, briefs, and the undercover-second-year play; admits he knew of Suzune since soon after enrollment.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> The man he wants removed or obstructed; student-council expulsions and exam design as the threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Calls her incompetent and a shadow-chaser; would cooperate if she joined the council — harsh, not indifferent.<span class=\"pg\">p.88–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Coconspirator by Ayanokōji’s framing; blocked the snow feint; “you aren’t fit to serve on the student council.”<span class=\"pg\">p.85–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> Secretary context via the brief handoff (Kushida later calls her).<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Blocks Ryuuen’s jab with vision obscured; adjusts glasses, unfazed.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the stair witness after the roof<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p117-1\">→ After: Ch.5: the debt behind the arm-grab<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p117-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 5  the debt behind the arm grab named as the relay rival ayanokoji beat  later as sibling and nagumo s rival  passing mention   you were even quicker than the student council president    satou on the relay  passing mention   they definitely weren t as dour as horikita    suzune  not manabu  passing mention  nagumo fixated on ayanokoji because of  horikita senpai  passing mention  nagumo removed anyone who stood in his way   manabu s earlier brief restated  passing mention   dialogue  sibling of suzune  debt from the rooftop  mission to remove nagumo  rival  his talking to ayanokoji triggers the theater approach  sibling link revealed to karuizawa as why manabu notices ayanokoji  debt and mission  karuizawa learns the arrangement","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: the debt behind the arm-grab<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.117, 119–126, 131–132, 140–141, 145, 151–153<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the relay rival Ayanokōji beat; later as sibling and Nagumo’s rival.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “you were even quicker than the student council president!” — Satou on the relay.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “They definitely weren’t as dour as Horikita.” — Suzune, not Manabu.<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Nagumo fixated on Ayanokōji because of “Horikita-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123–125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Nagumo removed anyone who stood in his way — Manabu’s earlier brief restated.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention / dialogue: sibling of Suzune; debt from the rooftop; mission to remove Nagumo.<span class=\"pg\">p.145, 151–153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Rival; his talking to Ayanokōji triggers the theater approach.<span class=\"pg\">p.125, 151–153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Sibling link revealed to Karuizawa as why Manabu notices Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Debt and mission; Karuizawa learns the arrangement.<span class=\"pg\">p.145, 151–153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p85-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the Nagumo debt and the sister test<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p124-1\">→ After: Ch.5: named in the relay callback<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p124-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"","w":"horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 5  named in the relay callback named once when nagumo identifies ayanokoji as the student who squared off against horikita senpai  passing mention   he was the student who squared off against horikita senpai in the relay race","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p124-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: named in the relay callback<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.124<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once when Nagumo identifies Ayanokōji as the student who squared off against Horikita-senpai.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “He was the student who squared off against Horikita-senpai in the relay race.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p117-1\">← Before: Ch.5: the debt behind the arm-grab<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p155-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the senpai the intel is for<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p155-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"","w":"kiriyama-ikuto nagumo-miyabi horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6  the senpai the intel is for named as kiriyama s admired class a senpai  intended recipient if nagumo is removed  passing mention   i joined the student council because i admired horikita senpai  passing mention  intel handoff plan  kiriyama still holds school rules in high respect because of horikita s endorsement  former class a senpai  the reason kiriyama approaches first years at all  the rival whose fall kiriyama wants horikita to exploit","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p155-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the senpai the intel is for<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.155–159<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as Kiriyama’s admired Class A senpai; intended recipient if Nagumo is removed.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “I joined the student council because I admired Horikita-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: intel handoff plan; Kiriyama still holds school rules in high respect because of Horikita’s endorsement.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> Former Class A senpai; the reason Kiriyama approaches first years at all.<span class=\"pg\">p.155–159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> The rival whose fall Kiriyama wants Horikita to exploit.<span class=\"pg\">p.155–159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v7_5-p124-1\">← Before: Ch.5: named in the relay callback<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p10-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"inner","w":"nagumo-miyabi horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 1  the graduation soliloquy retrospective first person soliloquy at graduation  his aimless excellence  the role model posture  nagumo s pressure  and the regret of never trusting a friend  detached self audit    i didn t know what i truly wanted out of life  prefers tasks assigned over drama  chose the school without ambition   setting an  example  being a  role model    the posture he now doubts   i realized my mistake and the regret that it had left me with  and  i realized  that this was just the beginning  nagumo  continues to take direct action against me  trying to clear me from his path    described as  a bulldozer  at graduation  gave up acting against nagumo before the end  no friend truly trusted from the bottom of his heart","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: the graduation soliloquy<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.10<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Retrospective first-person soliloquy at graduation: his aimless excellence, the role-model posture, Nagumo’s pressure, and the regret of never trusting a friend.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">“I realized my mistake—and the regret that it had left me with. And, I realized, that this was just the beginning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Detached self-audit — “I didn’t know what I truly wanted out of life”; prefers tasks assigned over drama.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Chose the school without ambition; “Setting an ‘example.’ Being a ‘role model.’” — the posture he now doubts.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Nagumo “continues to take direct action against me, trying to clear me from his path” — described as “a bulldozer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> At graduation: gave up acting against Nagumo before the end; no friend truly trusted from the bottom of his heart.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2: the duel conditions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p52-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi fujimaki horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 2  the duel conditions third year side of nagumo s early draft  later accepts the personal challenge under strict limits   i don t  this is more convenient for us too    on moving the large group draft up  accepts the average score duel  refuses nagumo s framing about which of them can get the most students expelled  forbids attacks on his pawns and any harm spilling to other students   competition invalid if nagumo meddles elsewhere   very well  i accept   however  this is a personal battle between you and me  don t drag anyone else into it  keeps the third years back when nagumo goads fujimaki into fighting  silence on whether pride is on the line   ayanokoji reads it as not intending to put pride on the line at all","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the duel conditions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.52–60<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Third-year side of Nagumo’s early draft; later accepts the personal challenge under strict limits.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"fujimaki.html\">Fujimaki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t. This is more convenient for us too.” — on moving the large-group draft up.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Very well. I accept.”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“However, this is a personal battle between you and me. Don’t drag anyone else into it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Accepts the average-score duel; refuses Nagumo’s framing about which of them can get the most students expelled; forbids attacks on his pawns and any harm spilling to other students — competition invalid if Nagumo meddles elsewhere.<span class=\"pg\">p.53, 57–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Fujimaki<\/b> Keeps the third-years back when Nagumo goads Fujimaki into fighting.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Silence on whether pride is on the line — Ayanokōji reads it as not intending to put pride on the line at all.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p10-1\">← Before: Ch.1: the graduation soliloquy<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p98-1\">→ After: Ch.3: named in Nagumo’s card-room frame<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p98-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi ishikura horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 3  named in nagumo s card room frame not on the page  named twice as the student council tension behind nagumo s third year party  passing mention   they probably knew of the tension between nagumo and horikita manabu and didn t want to get involved  passing mention  ishikura to nagumo    i don t like you picking fights with horikita  the open feud with the former president frames why some third years refuse to engage and why ishikura calls the card visit a fight  ishikura s rebuke is aimed at nagumo s horikita campaign  not at anything on the page","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p98-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: named in Nagumo’s card-room frame<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.98, 102<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Not on the page; named twice as the student-council tension behind Nagumo’s third-year party.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"ishikura.html\">Ishikura<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “They probably knew of the tension between Nagumo and Horikita Manabu and didn’t want to get involved.”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Ishikura to Nagumo — “I don’t like you picking fights with Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> The open feud with the former president frames why some third-years refuse to engage and why Ishikura calls the card visit a fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.98, 102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishikura<\/b> Ishikura’s rebuke is aimed at Nagumo’s Horikita campaign, not at anything on the page.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the duel conditions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.4: named as the genius in the way<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p116-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi ishikura kiriyama-ikuto horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 4  named as the genius in the way named in kiriyama s backstory line  p 118 119 named as nagumo s blocker for ishikura  passing mention  kiriyama s demotion history    horikita s brother had put us both in touch  passing mention  nagumo to ishikura    there s a genius like horikita manabu in your way  the three year campaign target  nagumo claims many ways to crush him whether or not he is representative  ishikura accepts the class b gap without taking nagumo s manabu removal frame  the brother connection that put kiriyama and ayanokoji in touch","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: named as the genius in the way<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.116, 118–119<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Kiriyama’s backstory line; p.118–119 named as Nagumo’s blocker for Ishikura.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"ishikura.html\">Ishikura<\/a> · <a href=\"kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Kiriyama’s demotion history — “Horikita’s brother had put us both in touch.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Nagumo to Ishikura — “there’s a genius like Horikita Manabu in your way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> The three-year campaign target; Nagumo claims many ways to crush him whether or not he is representative.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishikura<\/b> Ishikura accepts the Class B gap without taking Nagumo’s Manabu-removal frame.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> The brother-connection that put Kiriyama and Ayanokōji in touch.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p98-1\">← Before: Ch.3: named in Nagumo’s card-room frame<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p145-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the corridor meeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p145-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka ishikura tsunoda horikita-suzune horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 4  the corridor meeting morse light and a  25  note lead to a pitch black corridor meeting with ayanokoji about nagumo and the exam   do you know why i called you here   nagumo shows no mercy to those who defy him  he s employed underhanded methods like ryuuen more than once  he s also directly responsible for the second years  unusually high expulsion rate  however  he s never once broken a promise   this has been a waste of time  apparently   the student council can influence the special exams  the council is supposed to represent the students  perspectives and can therefore make significant revisions to penalties or meddle with the rules  however  the council cannot make these decisions on a whim  anxious about nagumo s public challenge and unexplained lesson laxity  certain nagumo never breaks a promise after two years on the council together  risks the conspicuous contact for nagumo intel and the bus message answer  leaves calling it a waste of time  ayanokoji infers ishikura or tsunoda helped place the bed note   manabu does not confirm  same inference as ishikura for who knew ayanokoji s bed  student council can revise penalties or meddle with exam rules   but not on a whim    not on these pages as speaker","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p145-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the corridor meeting<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.145–147<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Morse light and a “25” note lead to a pitch-black corridor meeting with Ayanokōji about Nagumo and the exam.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ishikura.html\">Ishikura<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#tsunoda\">Tsunoda<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you know why I called you here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Nagumo shows no mercy to those who defy him. He’s employed underhanded methods like Ryuuen more than once. He’s also directly responsible for the second-years’ unusually high expulsion rate. However, he’s never once broken a…”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“This has been a waste of time, apparently,”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nagumo shows no mercy to those who defy him. He’s employed underhanded methods like Ryuuen more than once. He’s also directly responsible for the second-years’ unusually high expulsion rate. However, he’s never once broken a promise.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The student council can influence the special exams. The council is supposed to represent the students’ perspectives and can therefore make significant revisions to penalties or meddle with the rules. However, the council cannot make these decisions on a whim.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Anxious about Nagumo’s public challenge and unexplained lesson laxity; certain Nagumo never breaks a promise after two years on the council together.<span class=\"pg\">p.145–147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Risks the conspicuous contact for Nagumo intel and the bus-message answer; leaves calling it a waste of time.<span class=\"pg\">p.145–147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishikura<\/b> Ayanokōji infers Ishikura or Tsunoda helped place the bed note — Manabu does not confirm.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsunoda<\/b> Same inference as Ishikura for who knew Ayanokōji’s bed.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Student council can revise penalties or meddle with exam rules — but not on a whim.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> — not on these pages as speaker.<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.4: named as the genius in the way<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p173-1\">→ After: Ch.6 half 2: the brother under the Nagumo lens<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p173-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi tachibana-akane ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6 half 2  the brother under the nagumo lens named as the reason for the second year probe  p 180 181 inside asahina s account   i needed to confirm nagumo s true intentions toward horikita s brother  asahina  nagumo made horikita senpai a goal  jealous of the missed relay challenge  tachibana is his secretary in the girls  large group   their representative is a different person  asahina  traps in the girls  group  won t have any effect on horikita senpai and miyabi s fight  the rivalry asahina describes   fair square on nagumo s side of the promise  secretary named in the group topology  the outsider reading both men through asahina and his own contact limits  placed trust in what nagumo said  parallel to ayanokoji s read of manabu s trust","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p173-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 half 2: the brother under the Nagumo lens<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.173, 180–181<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the reason for the second-year probe; p.180–181 inside Asahina’s account.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"tachibana-akane.html\">Tachibana Akane<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “I needed to confirm Nagumo’s true intentions toward Horikita’s brother.”<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Asahina: Nagumo made Horikita-senpai a goal; jealous of the missed relay challenge.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Tachibana is his secretary in the girls’ large group; “their representative is a different person.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Asahina: traps in the girls’ group “won’t have any effect on Horikita-senpai and Miyabi’s fight.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> The rivalry Asahina describes — fair square on Nagumo’s side of the promise.<span class=\"pg\">p.176, 181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> Secretary named in the group topology.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The outsider reading both men through Asahina and his own contact limits.<span class=\"pg\">p.173, 180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Placed trust in what Nagumo said (parallel to Ayanokōji’s read of Manabu’s trust).<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v8-p145-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the corridor meeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
